Portal | java: Incoming requests can now be traced with the OpenTelemetry Java agent.
Every request becomes one trace, which contains the requests to Mesh, to Mesh plugins
and to Keycloak, the page cache lookup and the template rendering. Background work,
the monitoring endpoints, static files, FormGen app files and requests of the
Blackbox exporter are not traced. This needs the new agent extension
@com.gentics.mesh.portal:mesh-portal-otel-extension@ in the portal image and
@OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=gentics_portal_java@. Traced responses contain the header
@X-Trace-Id@, the request span contains the ID of the logged in user (@user.id@),
and the default logging configuration prints the trace ID.
See the "documentation":https://www.gentics.com/guides/latest/portal-java/features/tracing.html for details.
